# Trivy allowlist — accepted vulnerability findings.
#
# The Security Scan workflow (.github/workflows/security-scan.yml) FAILS the
# build on HIGH/CRITICAL findings. To accept a finding (e.g. a transitive dep
# with no fix yet, or one not reachable in our usage), add its ID below with a
# justification and a review date. Keep this list SHORT and reviewed — see
# SECURITY_MAINTENANCE.md.
#
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line (CVE-xxxx-xxxx or GHSA-xxxx). Example:
#
#   # CVE-2024-99999 — <package>: not reachable, no fix upstream.
#   #   Accepted 2026-07-25 by <name>; re-review 2026-10-25.
#   CVE-2024-99999
#
# CVE-2024-23342 — ecdsa: vulnerable to the Minerva timing attack on P-256.
#   Same advisory pip-audit reports as PYSEC-2026-1325 (different ID scheme), so
#   it must be listed in BOTH allowlists.
#   NO FIX EXISTS — upstream considers side-channel attacks out of scope.
#   NOT REACHABLE HERE: `ecdsa` is a transitive dependency of python-jose only,
#   and we sign JWTs with HS256 (symmetric HMAC — see app/config.py), so the
#   affected ecdsa.SigningKey.sign_digest() / P-256 code path is never called.
#   Accepted 2026-07-26; re-review 2026-10-26. See SECURITY_MAINTENANCE.md.
CVE-2024-23342
